---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import Formula from '../../../components/Formula.astro';

const f = {
  fwd: "$$\\text{ml} = \\text{tsp} \\times 4.92892$$",
  rev: "$$\\text{tsp} = \\text{ml} \\div 4.92892$$",
};

const tocItems = [
  { id: 'how-to-use',      label: 'How to use this converter' },
  { id: 'formula',         label: 'How to convert teaspoons to ml' },
  { id: 'reference-table', label: 'Teaspoons to ml reference table' },
  { id: 'faq',             label: 'FAQs' },
  { id: 'related-tools',   label: 'Related tools' },
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "Teaspoons to Milliliters Converter",
    "url": "https://calculations.tools/conversion/volume-converter/tsp-to-ml",
    "description": "Convert teaspoons to milliliters for cooking and medicine. 1 teaspoon = 4.93 ml (US), 2 tsp = 9.86 ml, 1 tablespoon = 3 teaspoons = 14.79 ml.",
    "applicationCategory": "UtilitiesApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "Any",
    "browserRequirements": "Requires JavaScript",
    "isAccessibleForFree": true,
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "HowTo",
    "name": "How to convert teaspoons to milliliters",
    "description": "Multiply teaspoons by 4.92892 to get milliliters.",
    "step": [
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 1, "name": "Enter teaspoon value", "text": "Type your teaspoon value in the tsp field. The ml result updates instantly." },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 2, "name": "Read the result", "text": "The converted ml value appears. For 1 tsp, the result is 4.93 ml." },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 3, "name": "Convert in reverse", "text": "Type in the ml field to convert back to teaspoons." }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many ml is 1 teaspoon?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "1 US teaspoon equals 4.92892 ml, commonly rounded to 5 ml. Medical dosing often uses 5 ml as the standard teaspoon measurement." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is 5 ml equal to 1 teaspoon?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "5 ml is approximately 1 teaspoon. The exact US teaspoon is 4.929 ml. 5 ml is 1.4% larger. Medical spoons and dosing cups are calibrated to 5 ml." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many ml is 2 teaspoons?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "2 teaspoons equals 9.858 ml. Multiply 2 by 4.92892: 2 × 4.92892 = 9.858 ml. Often rounded to 10 ml in medicine." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many teaspoons is 10 ml?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "10 ml equals 2.029 teaspoons - about 2 teaspoons. Medical liquid doses of 10 ml are described as 2 teaspoons." } }
    ]
  }
];
---
<CalculatorLayout
  title="Teaspoons to Milliliters Converter"
  metaTitle="Teaspoons to Milliliters Converter | Convert tsp to ml"
  description="Convert teaspoons to ml for cooking and medicine. 1 tsp = 4.93 ml (5 ml in medicine), 2 tsp = 9.86 ml, 3 tsp = 1 tablespoon = 14.79 ml."
  canonical="https://calculations.tools/conversion/volume-converter/tsp-to-ml"
  tocItems={tocItems}
  embedSlug="tsp-to-ml"
  schema={schema}
  ogFormula="ml = tsp × 4.92892"
  ogExample="1 tsp = 4.93 ml (≈ 5 ml)"
>
  <div slot="calculator">
    <section class="calculator-interface">
      <div class="calculator-container">
        <div class="calculator-header">
          <h2>Instantly Convert tsp to ml</h2>
          <p>Type in either field - converts instantly in both directions</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pair-inputs">
          <div class="pair-field">
            <label for="lp-a">Teaspoons (tsp)</label>
            <input id="lp-a" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 1" />
          </div>
          <div class="pair-eq">=</div>
          <div class="pair-field">
            <label for="lp-b">Milliliters (ml)</label>
            <input id="lp-b" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 4.93" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pair-formula-note">1 tsp = 4.92892 ml &nbsp;·&nbsp; US teaspoon</div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <script src="/js/tsp-to-ml.js" is:inline></script>
  </div>
  <div slot="content">
    <div class="seo-container">
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-box-label">Quick answer</div>
        <p>To convert teaspoons to milliliters, multiply by <strong>4.92892</strong>. So 1 tsp = 4.93 ml, 2 tsp = 9.86 ml, and 3 tsp = 14.79 ml (1 tablespoon). In medicine, 1 teaspoon is standardized to 5 ml exactly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-box-label">Key takeaways</div>
        <ul>
          <li>Formula: ml = tsp × 4.92892. Quick estimate: 1 tsp ≈ 5 ml (medical standard).</li>
          <li>3 tsp = 1 tablespoon = 14.79 ml. 6 tsp = 2 tbsp = 1 fl oz = 29.57 ml.</li>
          <li>Medicine uses 5 ml per teaspoon for dosing. Recipes may specify 4.93 or 5 ml - both are correct in context.</li>
          <li>Reverse: tsp = ml ÷ 4.92892.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <h2 id="how-to-use">How to use our tsp to ml converter</h2>
      <p>Type any teaspoon value in the tsp field and the ml result appears instantly. Use decimals for partial teaspoons (0.5 for half a teaspoon). Both directions work without pressing a button.</p>
      <h2 id="formula">How do you convert teaspoons to ml?</h2>
      <p>Multiply the number of teaspoons by 4.92892. The US teaspoon is defined as exactly 1/3 of a tablespoon = 14.7868/3 = 4.92892 ml. For medicine, the standard is 5 ml per teaspoon as defined by the US FDA for over-the-counter labeling.</p>
      <Formula expr={f.fwd} />
      <p>Worked examples: 1/4 tsp = 1.23 ml. 1/2 tsp = 2.46 ml. 1 tsp = 4.93 ml. 2 tsp = 9.86 ml. 3 tsp = 14.79 ml. 6 tsp = 29.57 ml. 12 tsp = 59.15 ml (1/4 cup).</p>
      <h2 id="reference-table">Teaspoons to ml reference table</h2>
      <p>Teaspoon fractions and multiples converted to ml, with tablespoon and cup equivalents:</p>
      <div class="responsive-table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Teaspoons</th><th>Milliliters</th><th>Equivalent</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1/4 tsp</td><td>1.23 ml</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>1/2 tsp</td><td>2.46 ml</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3/4 tsp</td><td>3.70 ml</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>1 tsp</td><td>4.93 ml</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>1.5 tsp</td><td>7.39 ml</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2 tsp</td><td>9.86 ml</td><td>-</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3 tsp</td><td>14.79 ml</td><td>1 tablespoon</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6 tsp</td><td>29.57 ml</td><td>2 tbsp / 1 fl oz</td></tr>
            <tr><td>12 tsp</td><td>59.15 ml</td><td>4 tbsp / 1/4 cup</td></tr>
            <tr><td>24 tsp</td><td>118.3 ml</td><td>8 tbsp / 1/2 cup</td></tr>
            <tr><td>48 tsp</td><td>236.6 ml</td><td>16 tbsp / 1 cup</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h2 id="faq">FAQs about tsp to ml conversion</h2>
      <h3>How many ml is 1 teaspoon?</h3>
      <p>1 US teaspoon equals 4.92892 ml. In cooking, this is usually rounded to 5 ml. For medical liquid dosing, 5 ml is the official teaspoon standard per FDA labeling guidelines.</p>
      <h3>Is 5 ml equal to 1 teaspoon?</h3>
      <p>5 ml is approximately 1 teaspoon, but not exactly. The US teaspoon is 4.929 ml. 5 ml is 1.4% larger. Medical dosing cups are calibrated to 5 ml per teaspoon. For cooking, the difference is negligible.</p>
      <h3>How many ml is 2 teaspoons?</h3>
      <p>2 teaspoons equals 9.858 ml. This is often rounded to 10 ml in liquid medicine dosing instructions.</p>
      <h3>How many teaspoons is 10 ml?</h3>
      <p>10 ml equals 2.029 teaspoons - essentially 2 teaspoons. Many liquid medicines specify a 10 ml dose, described as 2 teaspoons on the label.</p>
      <h2 id="related-tools">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="related-tools-list">
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/ml-to-tsp">Milliliters to Teaspoons</a>
            <p>Reverse conversion - enter ml and get teaspoons instantly.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/tbsp-to-ml">Tablespoons to Milliliters</a>
            <p>Convert tablespoons to ml - 1 tbsp = 3 tsp = 14.79 ml.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/cup-to-ml">Cups to Milliliters</a>
            <p>Convert cups to ml - 1 cup = 48 teaspoons = 236.6 ml.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter">Volume Converter (all units)</a>
            <p>Convert between all volume units - ml, L, fl oz, cups, gallons, and more.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</CalculatorLayout>
<style is:global>
  .pair-inputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .pair-field label { display: block; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pair-field input { width: 100%; padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-radius: 8px; color: white; font-size: 1rem; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .pair-eq { font-size: 1.5rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pair-formula-note { text-align: center; font-size: 0.75rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45); margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .pair-inputs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .pair-eq { text-align: center; padding-bottom: 0; } }
</style>